 5. + This 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Mady again. Will we start saying AI;DR, as in, AI, didn't read? 

 That's the question on my mind after a viral Substack post points out that Amazon's famed six-page memo is no longer as useful because it's been turned into AI slop. One engineer began tagging AI-generated memos with "AI;DR" to indicate he wouldn't be reading them. His agent could just read and summarize those instead. 
 
